From a6267bff2a387e4757f28b6a5962e9e85015e389 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:57:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Objects returned by the connector now carry the connector

connector.get_projects()? followed by project.delete() failed with
MissingConnector, because get_projects/get_project/create_project,
get_templates/get_template/create_template/update_template and
get_nodes/get_node/get_links/get_link returned objects with no
connector attached.

These methods now take self: &Arc<Self> and attach the connector to
everything they return, through one private helper. Calling them on an
Arc<Gns3Connector> (also through a Lazy/static wrapper) is unchanged;
they can no longer be called on a bare, non-Arc Gns3Connector.

- tests/bound_objects.rs: regression tests, including the delete loop
  from the bug report (verified failing before the fix)
- tests/connector.rs: hold the connector in an Arc; two assertions had
  encoded the old behaviour (connector.is_none()) and now check is_some()
- Template::list/find delegate to the connector
- README: connector calls return typed structs (was: raw Value)
